# Project Description - CSR Matching Application 
In this project, your team is asked to design and develop a system to match Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) corporate volunteers (CV) to the person-in-need (PIN). Each company will have a main CSR Representative (on behalf of the CVs) to connect with the PIN.

Your main task is to create an application which satisfies all defined user stories

# Project Requirements
- Follow the Boundary-Controller-Entity framework.
- Adopt test-driven development i.e. test plans, test cases (include unit test cases)
- The system should have 100 synthetic user data in total comprising of all user types

## Access & Security Concepts

### **1. User Account (Identity)**

- **Definition:**  
  Represents a *unique digital identity* within the CSR Application, associated with a single person or organization.

- **Contains:**  
  Personal details (e.g. name, email, contact number), authentication credentials (username, password), and system metadata (account status, last login, creation date).

- **Purpose:**  
  Enables authentication (login) and identification of the user.

> 🧩 Analogy: The *User Account* is the “who” — the identity in the system.

---

### **2. User Profile (Authorization Context)**

- **Definition:**  
  Defines the *role or set of roles* assigned to a user account, which determines their access rights and functional scope in the system.

- **Contains:**
  - Role(s) assigned (e.g., CSR Representative, Platform Manager)
  - Associated permissions (e.g., View Reports, Manage Users)
  - Organizational context (e.g., Company, Region, Project group)

- **Purpose:**  
  Translates *who the user is* into *what they are allowed to do*.

> 🧩 Analogy: The *User Profile* is the “what” — the authorization layer.

---

### **3. Roles (Functional Roles in the System)**

Each role groups related permissions and responsibilities.

| **Role** | **Description** | **Key Permissions / Responsibilities** |
|-----------|------------------|----------------------------------------|
| **CSR Representative** | Acts as the main contact person from a corporate partner. Connects with Persons-In-Need (PINs) to coordinate volunteer activities and support delivery. | - View and manage assigned PINs |
| **Person-In-Need (PIN)** | Recipient of assistance under CSR initiatives. Connects with CSR Representatives to request and receive help. | - Create and update personal requests<br>- View assigned CSR Representative<br>- Acknowledge receipt of assistance |
| **User Administrator (User Admin)** | Responsible for managing user lifecycle and access privileges within the CSR system. | - Create, update, deactivate user accounts<br>- Assign roles and reset passwords<br>- Review user access reports |
| **Platform Manager** | Oversees platform-level configuration, service categorization, and reporting. Ensures operational data integrity. | - Manage volunteer service categories<br>- View system-wide statistics and reports (daily, weekly, monthly)<br>- Configure system parameters and settings |

